course: dictionary
lesson: 14429
title: Overwhelming
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Overwhelming describes something so big, strong or heavy that it is hard to deal with. You can often work out its meaning from the words around it. «The waves were overwhelming, and the small boat was pushed back to the shore.» Small boats cannot fight huge waves, so overwhelming must mean very strong and too much to fight against.
explain: The same word can describe a feeling. «Sam felt an overwhelming sadness when his best friend moved away.» Sadness that is overwhelming is so strong that it is hard to cope with. When someone feels overwhelmed, they feel that something is too much for them to cope with.
explain: Overwhelming can also describe a very large number. «The team won the vote by an overwhelming majority.» A majority is the bigger group. If the win was overwhelming, the winners were far ahead, not just a little. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Overwhelming means very great or strong, so that it is hard to deal with.
fact: «Overwhelming majority» means a very large amount more than the other side.
fact: «Feel overwhelmed» means feel that something is too much to cope with.
fact: Breaking a big task into small steps can make an overwhelming job feel easier, and talking to someone you trust can help too.
fact: Overwhelming is the -ing form of the verb overwhelm: overwhelm, overwhelms, overwhelmed, overwhelming.
exercise: «The waves were overwhelming, and the small boat was pushed back to the shore.» What does overwhelming mean here? | Bright and colourful | *Very strong and too much to fight against | Gentle and calm | Very small and quiet
exercise: The team won the vote by an overwhelming majority. What does this mean? | *By a very large amount | By one vote only | The votes were lost in the post | Nobody voted at all
exercise: Sam says, «My homework feels overwhelming.» What does he most likely mean? | *It is too much for him to cope with | He has finished everything | He likes maths | He wants to do more homework
test: «Her feelings were overwhelming after the big goodbye.» Which word could replace overwhelming without changing the meaning? | funny | tiny | *too strong to cope with | boring
test: Lia felt overwhelmed by the noise of the crowd. What does overwhelmed mean here? | Felt happy and calm | Felt sleepy | Felt very cold | *Felt that it was too much to cope with
exam: Which phrase best matches «an overwhelming majority»? | Only a few people | *By a very large number | A small group of friends | Nobody at all
